WEBVTT

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:18.000
<v Programme Office>Welcome everyone to week four. Today is about taking AI prototypes to production. We'll finish with hackathon logistics.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:40.000
<v Dr. Thabo Dlamini>Three things kill prototypes: no owner after the demo, no monitoring, and no plan for data privacy. Pick one person who owns the thing after launch.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:06:10.000
<v Dr. Thabo Dlamini>For chatbots over group data, tell people what is collected, keep it inside the group, and give an easy way to remove sources. Log questions the bot could not answer so you can fix gaps.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:10:20.000
<v Dr. Thabo Dlamini>My deployment checklist: environment variables for secrets, a health check, backups of the database, a README anyone can follow, and a cost estimate per month.

00:31:02.000 --> 00:31:40.000
<v Programme Office>Hackathon logistics. Submissions close Thursday 24 September at 23:59 SAST. Send your repo link and setup notes to the programme email with subject UniPods Hackathon Submission.

00:31:41.000 --> 00:32:15.000
<v Programme Office>Each team gets five minutes to demo on Monday 28 September at 14:00. The whole cohort votes. Criteria: does it work, is it useful for this group, is it easy to run, and how well it handles chats and calls.

00:32:20.000 --> 00:32:45.000
<v Sipho>Can we use paid APIs like Claude or OpenAI?

00:32:46.000 --> 00:33:05.000
<v Programme Office>Yes, any API is fine, but include a monthly cost estimate in your setup notes.

00:34:10.000 --> 00:34:40.000
<v Amara>Will the winning bot actually be added to the WhatsApp group?

00:34:41.000 --> 00:35:02.000
<v Programme Office>Yes, the winner will be deployed to the cohort group the week after demo day. Action item for all teams: make sure an admin can add new chat exports and recordings without touching code.
